# Who must review what.
#
# There is deliberately no `*` rule. Agents open and merge their own pull
# requests autonomously, and a catch-all owner would force the reviewer account
# onto every PR. Only paths that can change CI credentials, the published image
# or the release version need a named reviewer.
#
# Reviewer enforcement comes from "Require review from Code Owners" on `main`,
# which only counts approvals from the owners below.
#
# @KookyAgentReviewer is listed so the reviewer account can approve and merge
# these paths on its own: a PR author cannot approve its own PR, and here the
# author is @KookyAgent. Remove that account from a line to make the matching
# path human-review-only.

/.github/         @Kookster310 @KookyAgentReviewer
/docker/          @Kookster310 @KookyAgentReviewer
/pyproject.toml   @Kookster310 @KookyAgentReviewer
